.SS "void VERUM_ASCON_HASH256_digest (uint8_t * message, uint32_t message_size, uint32_t digest[8U])"

.PP
Ascon-Hash256 message digest\&. Computes the 256-bit digest of \fRmessage\fP using the Ascon-Hash256 sponge construction defined in Algorithm 7 of NIST SP 800-232 Section 5\&.1\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImessage\fP Input message buffer\&. May be \fRNULL\fP if and only if \fRmessage_size\fP is zero, in which case the hash of the empty string is computed\&. 
.br
\fImessage_size\fP Byte length of \fRmessage\fP\&. May be zero\&. 
.br
\fIdigest\fP Destination buffer for the 256-bit digest, written as eight consecutive 32-bit words\&. The caller is responsible for providing a buffer of at least eight words\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPrecondition\fP
.RS 4
\fRdigest\fP is non-NULL\&. 

.PP
\fRmessage\fP is non-NULL when \fRmessage_size\fP is greater than zero\&. 

.PP
\fRmessage\fP points to a readable buffer of at least \fRmessage_size\fP bytes\&. 

.PP
\fRmessage\fP and \fRdigest\fP do not overlap\&. 
.RE
.PP

